<title>USA: U.S. May wholesale inventories rose 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. May wholesale inventories rose 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department report of</p>
<p>wholesale inventories and sales, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p> (Percent Changes)	May    Apr--Rev from  May97/96</p>
<p> Inventories Total	0.2   -0.5    -0.7	0.8</p>
<p> Sales Total		0.2   -0.1    UNCH	5.1</p>
<p> (Billions of dollars)    May     Apr--Rev from   May96</p>
<p> Inventories Total   258.68  258.05  257.64   256.74</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	165.24  164.45  164.03   160.92</p>
<p> --Cars/Parts	   26.85   26.42   26.35    27.16</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   93.44   93.60   93.61    95.82</p>
<p> --Petroleum Prods.    5.23    5.18    5.14     4.91</p>
<p> (Billions of dollars)    May     Apr--Rev from   May96</p>
<p>  Sales Total	  210.35  209.93  210.19   200.08</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	108.17  108.75  108.84   103.58</p>
<p> --Cars/Parts	   18.12   17.94   18.07    17.14</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods  102.18  101.18  101.35    96.50</p>
<p> --Petroleum Prods.   14.49   14.46   14.61    14.51</p>
<p>The May stock-to-sales ratio for merchant wholesalers, seasonally adjusted, was 1.23 months' worth, the same as in April and in March.</p>
<p>The ratio is a measure of how many months it would take to sell existing inventories at the current sales pace.</p>
</text>
